ving the  right people around you can help but  ultimately the culture in number 10 and  the decisions the government makes come  from the top and the prime minister  himself  if he's going to stay in office is going  to have to change the way he is behaving  and running the government  isn't the problem here then  i speak to you as an experienced advisor  that actually  he doesn't take advice and you could  have socrates machiavelli  and whoever else you liked in there uh  to advice him  but he when he's got it in his head  won't take that advice cannot help  himself and he will do what he wants  isn't the problem here it's not the  advisors not the circle around him it's  the prime minister so that that  definitely has been the problem and the  question is whether it's going to change  the other person that he's  bringing back into number uh bringing in  to number 10 is the new director of  communications good harry who was one of  his key advisors when he was mayor of  london so there was a period as you all  know from your own experience  when he was running london where first  with simon milton then with eddie lister  he had a team around him that he did  seem to to listen to and respect so it  is possible  uh that these changes you know he might  pay more attention to this new team than  he was to the previous one but you're  absolutely right about what the problem  has been up until now  uh it it  i don't want to take too much time on  this specific point but  every time  one of these things happens you know  he says there was no party oh yes there  was a party uh i wasn't another party oh  yes i was at the party uh  there's whatever it is about kirsten  somebody says  uh he's going to change he says it's  going to change and then he does it all  over again  yes i think  at some point in the future when  someone's writing a book about how to  handle political scandals the events of  the last few months will be like chapter  one of how not to do it  now if you